=TITLE CHANGES 

=head1 Upcoming

=item leave test-directory samples out of the site: they are fixtures for other people's documentation generators, not documentation of the module. A README among them is still taken, since it describes the data around it

=item carry what a module declares next to the measured pages: the units it ships and what it leans on, so a rating computed later from a stored record can be reproduced

=item refuse to write a corpus record when a registry it reads is missing or does not parse, instead of storing one that says nobody declared anything

=item note whether a page shows the output of its example, the second of the two signs that tell a worked example from a bare snippet

=item list the selected files separated by NUL and skip the ones whose name holds a control character: one registry entry carries a newline inside its own name, which tore a path in two and lost the file without a word

=item name every file the parser could not read, instead of sending the whole complaint to nowhere

=item measure the corpus while parsing it: markup census with the module reach of every construct, per-page facts, unparsed files and the settings the numbers were taken under

=item take documentation out of module sources: a source file gets a page when its pod says something the README does not

=item declare the packages the repository's own scripts import, and restore the dependency tree after a site build detaches it

=item create the release before recording the snapshot, and let a failed snapshot push not fail the run

=item let a second data release on the same day get its own tag instead of failing

=item build a page for every module in the registry, including the 139 that ship no documentation
=item clean stray markdown and windows backslashes out of link targets on module pages
=item publish a data release weekly, not only on demand

=item link module names in the change report to their pages, for modules that have one

=item build and publish a dated data release from CI — site archive, offline bundle and server image, with the version diff as release notes

=item resolve a snapshot name against the snapshots directory whichever way it is given

=item fetch module sources over https — the git protocol they list has been switched off since 2022
=item stop the refresh when more than a twentieth of the module sources have no checkout at all; a checkout that merely failed to update is reported, not fatal

=item credit the tools in the site template footer, where the rest of the footer lives

=item record a dated snapshot of module versions on every data refresh, and compare two snapshots into release notes

=item stop storing generated corpus trees in the repository; a fast rebuild now says so when they are missing

=item document the offline bundle in the mcp server readme

=item bump the C<@podlite> toolchain to the v0.0.77 release
=item treat any url scheme as external, so links like irc: no longer get a section prefix
=item strip markdown left inside a link target; the parser now hands over the target itself
=item quote the module page url so names with spaces keep their full path
=item skip modules whose name carries control characters
=item reduce pages size up to 2-3 times
=item refactor components to use C<=include> feature

=head1 v1.0
=item1 official Raku project documentation
=item1 documentation for all user modules
=item1 collections of code examples
=item1 markdown files from various sources
=item1 global index of terms
=item1 global real-time search

